vkd3d-proton: overlap MoltenVK encoding and use uniform root CBVs

MoltenVK maps the shared Vulkan queue to an ordered Metal queue. Do not
CPU-wait after each same-priority mixed graphics/compute command buffer:
that prevents CPU encoding from overlapping GPU work. Preserve high-priority
staggering, CPU resolution of cross-queue fence waits, and all UMD drain and
kernel fence ordering. This is deliberately narrower than no_staggered_submit.

Use the existing uniform push-descriptor path for root CBVs on MoltenVK.
No volatile descriptor-table hoisting or shader math/robustness relaxation.
The bindless flags already participate in the shader interface cache key;
force_raw_va_cbv remains an explicit diagnostic override.

2026-10-03, M1 Max 24 GPU, Windows ARM64 4 vCPU/8 GiB, WLE 1.1 DX12:
6255 / 37.46 fps with uniform CBVs + MoltenVK 0142 and original submit policy;
7048 / 42.21 fps with this narrower submit policy and VKD3D_CONFIG empty
(+12.68%). Supplied unmodified baseline: 5126 / 30.70 fps. The broader
no_staggered_submit experiment on the baseline reached 6677 / 39.98 fps.
Root-CBV-only exploratory results 6760 / 40.48 and 6801 / 40.73 fps were
small; no isolated CBV gain is claimed. See docs/wle-performance-2026-10-03.md
for final repeated scores, correctness checks and residual gap.

